diff -ruN a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
--- a/CHANGELOG.md	2026-09-21 20:41:53.226456658 +0000
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md	2026-09-21 20:41:53.237168838 +0000
@@ -8,7 +8,15 @@
 - The locked feature-schema check no longer forces missing endpoints to be fabricated for wells with no usable signal; missing endpoints remain an error on wells that have signal.
 - Colab runner: restored the site/cell-type dataset detail on the `UNDOCUMENTED_PLATFORM_CODE` flag (the committed regression test was failing).
 
+### Changed (algorithm - requires a new validation version if frozen earlier)
+- Beat detection: the effective prominence is now max(`min_prominence_uv`, `noise_prominence_multiplier` x robust noise scale of the trace), default 10 robust SDs, so noise and small background deflections no longer become beats (real Cardio PyMEA window: precision 0.24-0.30 -> 1.00, beat rate 94-117 -> 29.3 bpm).
+- `beat_detection_rate` is two-sided (over-detection lowers it) and the rhythm search covers 15-120 bpm, halving a 2x period when the half-period is genuinely periodic.
+- Noise is estimated on the raw trace (it was measured after filtering and read about 50x too low, so the noise QC could never trigger).
+- The repolarization search window now extends to 1200 ms (still bounded by the next beat); FPD above 450 ms was previously unmeasurable. Repolarization-peak prominence follows the adaptive threshold.
+- `ElectrodeFeatures.fpd_stv_ms` reports classical repolarization STV for information only; the scored `stv` remains inter-beat-interval variability.
+
 ### Added
+- `pymea_beat_validation.py`: `--exclude` keeps algorithm-development regions out of the annotation sample, and `score` audits the default QC on the annotated windows (false rejections / bad admissions).
 - Cardio PyMEA real layout: `io.mcs_ascii` now reads the original MC_DataTool export unmodified (title line, blank line, names row, units row in latin-1; units verified), records units/header size in the lineage, and jumps to windows by byte offset in fixed-width files (position verified, streaming fallback). `scripts/validation/pymea_beat_validation.py` builds a blinded, seeded annotation sheet (raw-voltage plots only) and scores CardioScore's beat detector against one or two human annotators; `validation/signal_validation_criteria.yaml` holds draft acceptance criteria.
 - Signal-level validation: `validation.signal_accuracy` (event matching, precision/recall/F1, timing error, bias/MAE/RMSE/limits of agreement/Lin's CCC, deterministic-rebuild hashing), `validation.signal_truth` (synthetic recordings with exact truth), `scripts/validation/synthetic_signal_benchmark.py`, and `tests/test_signal_accuracy.py`, whose `xfail(strict=True)` tests document known extraction limits (FPD above 450 ms, noise estimate, over-detection not lowering `beat_detection_rate`).
 - `io.mcs_ascii` reader and `scripts/validation/adapt_cardio_pymea.py` for Multichannel Systems MC_Data ASCII exports (Cardio PyMEA): header located from the data, names never guessed, uniform-timestamp checks, requested electrode order preserved, twice-run hash verification.
