+    The strongest autocorrelation peak is taken first. A genuine rhythm also correlates with itself at
+    half that period whenever every other beat is weaker (alternans) or was missed by a threshold, so
+    the period is halved as long as a real peak (>= 0.05, about eight standard deviations of
+    chance autocorrelation for a 30 s recording) sits near the half-period. This keeps a 2x period from
+    hiding an every-other-beat detection failure while still covering slow rhythms up to ``hi_s``.
+    """
